\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overview of the HAACHAMA pipeline used to generate a deforming fish-shaped digital twin and a cylinder surrogate. Infrared video recordings provided the fish trajectory and body contour, and wall-mounted pressure sensors provided the only direct experimental access to the wake. The fish-shaped digital twin and the cylinder surrogate were driven by the same centre-of-mass trajectory.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:haachama}{{1}{2}{Overview of the HAACHAMA pipeline used to generate a deforming fish-shaped digital twin and a cylinder surrogate. Infrared video recordings provided the fish trajectory and body contour, and wall-mounted pressure sensors provided the only direct experimental access to the wake. The fish-shaped digital twin and the cylinder surrogate were driven by the same centre-of-mass trajectory}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:haachama@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][2][]2}}
